## 🔎 REVIEW MEMO — Three-Agent Gap Review (2026-08-12)

Three focused passes were performed using the Senior Software Architect, Investigator, and RANGER prompts.

- **Architecture:** the current auth boundary is page-level, not API-level. Most route handlers still resolve `DEV_TENANT_ID`; the `.env.example` tenant value is also not the UUID used by `src/lib/db/index.ts`, so session-derived tenancy is not yet a safe drop-in.
- **Investigator:** the recurring reliability weakness is uncorrelated `console.*` logging across API, worker, and library boundaries. The eBay webhook route also logs a full payload. Standardized correlation IDs, error classification, and redaction are required before production operations.
- **RANGER:** the highest-risk finding is missing explicit auth/RBAC on API/admin routes, especially `/api/admin/beta-users`, which accepts tenant and user identifiers from the request. This is recorded as ERR-016; no auth logic was changed because the prompt requires approval before changing authentication behavior.
- **Verification:** Vitest was attempted but failed during config startup with an environment access error, so test execution remains unverified in this workspace.

Actions are tracked in `tasks/todo.md`; the error and pattern registers contain ERR-016 through ERR-018. The next safe implementation slice is a shared server-side authorization helper plus route-by-route migration and cross-tenant tests.
